Really want to do this right now?

00:32:25.970 --> 00:32:26.930
Oh, yeah, I think so.

00:32:28.220 --> 00:32:29.820
What the hell's going on with you? Are you drunk?

00:32:30.310 --> 00:32:30.850
Not enough.

00:32:31.270 --> 00:32:32.510
But you know, hey, we can fix that.

00:32:32.870 --> 00:32:33.530
Touch me at Heineken.

00:32:33.930 --> 00:32:34.850
Oh, you think this is funny?

00:32:36.010 --> 00:32:37.110
It's bad enough that you drank.

00:32:37.190 --> 00:32:38.570
I don't think we're not going to talk about that,

00:32:38.650 --> 00:32:40.810
but you had to pick this weekend to turn into a teenager?

00:32:41.860 --> 00:32:43.740
You haven't been to a party since we got here

00:32:43.740 --> 00:32:45.680
and all of a sudden you're getting plastered and arrested?

00:32:46.950 --> 00:32:49.950
If you want to embarrass me in front of your grandparents, you have done one hell of a job.

00:32:50.030 --> 00:32:51.470
Yeah, that's exactly right.

00:32:51.720 --> 00:32:52.800
That's what this is about.

00:32:52.960 --> 00:32:53.940
This is all about you.

00:32:54.220 --> 00:32:57.460
I got arrested just so you could feel bad about yourself.

00:32:57.540 --> 00:32:58.880
No, damn well, that's not what I meant.

00:32:59.240 --> 00:32:59.520
Hey!

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.380
Look at me, I'm super dad.

00:33:01.680 --> 00:33:02.940
Let's fish and make waffles.

00:33:05.130 --> 00:33:06.430
I got news for you.

00:33:07.110 --> 00:33:09.030
They're not buying it, but don't worry.

00:33:10.010 --> 00:33:11.190
You promised to raise my allowance,

00:33:11.370 --> 00:33:13.600
I promise I'll give you a hug right in front of grandpa.

00:33:14.360 --> 00:33:17.020
All right, listen, I'm not gonna talk to you

00:33:17.020 --> 00:33:17.700
when you're like this.

00:33:18.420 --> 00:33:20.260
You go upstairs to bed and I'll talk to you in the morning.

00:33:20.660 --> 00:33:22.420
Okay, you know, maybe I should drink more often

00:33:22.420 --> 00:33:23.720
because not talking to me,

00:33:24.290 --> 00:33:26.960
that's the best idea you've ever had, ever.

00:33:31.460 --> 00:33:32.440
Thank you.

00:33:45.740 --> 00:33:45.940
Of course.

00:33:55.430 --> 00:33:55.650
me.

00:33:55.980 --> 00:33:56.980
Maybe if I pay you.

00:33:59.140 --> 00:33:59.960
It's not about that bad.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:00.960
your father's not interested.

00:34:01.240 --> 00:34:02.540
We have to make him interested.

00:34:02.700 --> 00:34:03.720
Well, it's just not that simple.

00:34:04.280 --> 00:34:05.260
Thank you.

00:34:07.510 --> 00:34:07.730
Look.

00:34:08.150 --> 00:34:08.690
It's my dad.

00:34:08.950 --> 00:34:10.270
Can't you just try one more time?

00:34:10.740 --> 00:34:11.080
for me.

00:34:18.870 --> 00:34:19.410
Well, thank you.

00:34:21.110 --> 00:34:23.410
If possible, she really wants four cartons of eggs.

00:34:24.060 --> 00:34:26.220
We don't question this, we just do its bidding.

00:34:28.730 --> 00:34:29.970
We'd better get you some...

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:30.600
Yes, but come on.

00:34:31.340 --> 00:34:31.980
for a new head.

00:34:32.460 --> 00:34:32.760
Thank you.

00:34:33.990 --> 00:34:36.410
You know, what you did last night was pretty stupid, you know that?

00:34:37.380 --> 00:34:39.340
He was being unreasonable. You saw him.

00:34:39.520 --> 00:34:41.000
Yeah, yeah, I'm not arguing that.

00:34:42.500 --> 00:34:42.600
Thank you.

00:34:44.460 --> 00:34:44.920
of the house.

00:34:46.020 --> 00:34:48.180
Getting drunk? That's childish. You're not a child.

00:34:48.400 --> 00:34:49.840
Yeah, he treats me like one.

00:34:49.940 --> 00:34:51.600
Don't let him. When I was a kid.

00:34:52.550 --> 00:34:53.670
We had no money, my family.

00:34:54.500 --> 00:34:57.680
I had to work every day after school just to put food on the table.

00:34:57.840 --> 00:34:59.500
Now it makes you grow up pretty fast.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.940
By the time I was 16, I was considered a man by my mother and father.

00:35:03.160 --> 00:35:05.340
And that was one of the greatest gifts they ever gave me.

00:35:06.790 --> 00:35:07.510
Know what I found out?

00:35:10.470 --> 00:35:11.490
Eating what you want is easy.

00:35:13.020 --> 00:35:14.640
Knowing what you want, that's the challenge.

00:35:15.660 --> 00:35:17.360
That's what separates the men from the boys.

00:35:18.690 --> 00:35:19.110
You understand?

00:35:19.620 --> 00:35:21.020
No, not really.

00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:22.880
Now let me try it this way.

00:35:24.440 --> 00:35:26.470
What do you want, Ephraim?

00:35:26.590 --> 00:35:29.900
I don't mean just permission to go to a party.

00:35:30.990 --> 00:35:33.760
Coming for your life right now.

00:35:33.860 --> 00:35:34.320
What do you want?

00:35:34.540 --> 00:35:35.000
What do you wish?

00:35:35.120 --> 00:35:41.820
We'll figure it out and make it happen.

00:35:44.270 --> 00:35:45.210
Oh, sorry.

00:35:48.520 --> 00:35:51.340
Is this your grandfather?

00:35:52.880 --> 00:35:53.520
Uh, yeah.

00:35:53.800 --> 00:35:54.400
Uh, Grandpa.

00:35:55.450 --> 00:35:56.230
This is Amy Abbott.

00:35:56.420 --> 00:35:57.000
Amy Abbott.

00:35:58.590 --> 00:35:59.310
Nice to meet you.

00:35:59.430 --> 00:35:59.890
Nice to meet you.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:00.980
Thank you.

00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:03.280
Look at this. I'll go get you some aspirin.

00:36:05.240 --> 00:36:05.660
It's on.

00:36:06.070 --> 00:36:07.790
Heard the cops busted up the party last night.

00:36:08.730 --> 00:36:08.950
Thank you.

00:36:11.380 --> 00:36:12.080
How long were you there?

00:36:13.940 --> 00:36:14.880
long enough to move on.

00:36:27.830 --> 00:36:27.990
Okay.

00:36:29.020 --> 00:36:30.000
Well, if you want the...

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:31.060
That's a good French toast.

00:36:31.560 --> 00:36:33.380
I'm going to have to make the challah from scratch.

00:36:34.410 --> 00:36:37.410
Your grandfather can't seem to find a Jewish bakery anywhere.

00:36:37.960 --> 00:36:38.380
Go figure.

00:36:39.180 --> 00:36:39.640
Can I help?

00:36:41.160 --> 00:36:43.820
Well, I thought you were going to finish doing the tires with Edna today.

00:36:44.020 --> 00:36:45.200
I can do that any time.

00:36:45.420 --> 00:36:46.580
I'd rather stay home with you.

00:36:49.670 --> 00:36:50.650
Thank you.

00:36:55.690 --> 00:36:57.850
your mother ever tell you her famous Shabbat story?

00:36:59.340 --> 00:36:59.820
I don't know.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:06.270
Uh, she was right around your age, and going to the yeshiva just a few blocks down from

00:37:06.270 --> 00:37:10.420
our house, and every Friday they would do a little Shabbat service.

00:37:10.660 --> 00:37:13.940
You know, light the candles, say the motzi, anyway.

00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:18.040
Every week, a different child would get to lead the prayer.

00:37:18.300 --> 00:37:19.780
Well, it was a big honor.

00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:22.730
And the week it was your mother's turn?

00:37:24.160 --> 00:37:25.300
That's all she could talk about.

00:37:25.540 --> 00:37:29.470
I spent an hour French braiding her hair that morning.

00:37:29.550 --> 00:37:29.930
I will...

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:30.880
I'll never forget it.

00:37:32.040 --> 00:37:32.280
So.

00:37:33.130 --> 00:37:34.570
The big moment finally comes.

00:37:35.650 --> 00:37:37.470
She walks up to the head of the table.

00:37:38.470 --> 00:37:43.570
And as soon as they pin the big doily on her head, she starts screaming.

00:37:44.170 --> 00:37:47.350
She wanted everyone to see her pretty French braid.

00:37:48.940 --> 00:37:49.520
So what happened?

00:37:51.370 --> 00:37:52.970
Dasi Pearl did the mozi.

00:37:54.020 --> 00:37:57.860
And your mother sat back down in her chair.

00:37:58.060 --> 00:37:59.480
And at the end of the prayer,

00:38:00.090 --> 00:38:07.440
smiled and said amen with the rest of the children no one could tell your mother what to do

00:38:07.440 --> 00:38:25.750
she was a she was a tough cookie am i doing it right you're doing it perfect tatala just perfect

00:38:37.740 --> 00:38:40.140
You just don't know when to stop, do you?

00:38:41.140 --> 00:38:42.620
Your son came to my house this morning.

00:38:46.540 --> 00:38:47.880
I'm sorry you shouldn't have done that.

00:38:48.260 --> 00:38:49.500
He's worried about you, Mike.

00:38:50.690 --> 00:38:51.610
Let me tell you something.

00:38:52.910 --> 00:38:55.770
I would give anything to have with my son what you have with yours.

00:38:56.310 --> 00:38:58.690
You have no idea how lucky you are.

00:39:00.640 --> 00:39:01.840
Yeah, me as a good kid.

00:39:02.020 --> 00:39:06.150
Then help him. Help him by taking care of yourself.

00:39:07.270 --> 00:39:09.560
Look, forget everything I said the other day.

00:39:09.600 --> 00:39:10.400
That's not what it's about.

00:39:10.860 --> 00:39:14.200
You need to have this surgery because your son needs you.

00:39:15.000 --> 00:39:15.680
It's as simple as that.

00:39:19.690 --> 00:39:20.030
Carrot.

00:39:21.200 --> 00:39:22.510
I know, it's natural.

00:39:23.500 --> 00:39:24.980
Not just about going under the knife.

00:39:25.100 --> 00:39:26.900
What if this doesn't work?

00:39:27.140 --> 00:39:29.540
I mean, what if I go through the whole thing, the operation,

00:39:29.780 --> 00:39:29.980
every single thing?

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:30.900
and nothing changes.

00:39:32.900 --> 00:39:33.960
I keep eating the same way.

00:39:35.590 --> 00:39:36.290
I don't think I could.

00:39:37.420 --> 00:39:38.440
I don't disappoint Ben like that.

00:39:42.920 --> 00:39:44.140
in front of him that way.

00:39:46.410 --> 00:39:48.530
If you don't try, you're still going to let him down.

00:39:49.640 --> 00:39:51.060
And ask for failing in front of your son.

00:39:52.140 --> 00:39:53.140
You're looking at the master.

00:39:54.220 --> 00:39:55.080
The good news is...

00:39:55.500 --> 00:39:56.680
It gets easier the more you do it.

00:39:57.700 --> 00:39:59.140
Why don't you give yourself a chance, my...

00:40:00.920 --> 00:40:01.800
Give Ben a chance.

00:40:06.460 --> 00:40:06.740
Ow.

00:40:09.180 --> 00:40:10.820
What's our plane ticket cost these days?

00:40:19.830 --> 00:40:20.310
What's going on?

00:40:22.170 --> 00:40:22.750
We're just talking.

00:40:24.470 --> 00:40:24.770
about.

00:40:26.300 --> 00:40:26.900
What, New York?

00:40:29.140 --> 00:40:29.900
are from coming

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:30.940
live there with us.

00:40:32.740 --> 00:40:33.360
Who brought this up?

00:40:34.540 --> 00:40:34.840
I did.

00:40:41.030 --> 00:40:41.390
I see.

00:40:46.980 --> 00:40:47.600
Give us a minute a little.

00:40:48.490 --> 00:40:48.870
It could be alright.

00:41:07.420 --> 00:41:07.860
What are you doing?

00:41:08.760 --> 00:41:09.380
This isn't me.

00:41:09.440 --> 00:41:10.220
Like hell it isn't.

00:41:11.030 --> 00:41:12.330
Do you think you decided something here?

00:41:13.180 --> 00:41:15.140
You think you're just going to take my son away from me?

00:41:15.510 --> 00:41:15.990
that hold it.

00:41:16.860 --> 00:41:17.980
We haven't made any decision.

00:41:19.060 --> 00:41:19.500
just talk.

00:41:19.860 --> 00:41:20.960
There's nothing to talk about.

00:41:21.560 --> 00:41:22.880
He's not doing well, Andy.

00:41:24.410 --> 00:41:26.430
Not here and not with you, and you know it too.

00:41:26.620 --> 00:41:28.360
Oh, you think he'll do better away from his family?

00:41:28.480 --> 00:41:28.960
Is that what you think?

00:41:29.080 --> 00:41:29.820
Hey, I'm his family.

00:41:30.410 --> 00:41:32.910
He spent more time with me in the last 15 years than he has with you.

00:41:33.860 --> 00:41:36.740
You think a couple of months in the mountains makes up for Missy most of his life?

00:41:38.280 --> 00:41:38.840
It doesn't.

00:41:42.950 --> 00:41:44.250
You and I are surgeons, Andy, right?

00:41:45.640 --> 00:41:46.480
We know how it's done.

00:41:47.850 --> 00:41:48.770
You locate the problem.

00:41:49.700 --> 00:41:50.260
We're going in.

00:41:50.790 --> 00:41:51.610
You excise it.

00:41:52.550 --> 00:41:53.150
You move on.

00:41:54.220 --> 00:41:55.040
What you don't do.

00:41:56.100 --> 00:41:57.680
is ignore it and pretend it'll go away.

00:41:57.680 --> 00:41:58.780
I'm not ignoring it.

00:42:06.170 --> 00:42:08.150
Look, we are doing better now.

00:42:09.060 --> 00:42:10.260
We are working things out.

00:42:10.790 --> 00:42:14.540
You have no idea how hard this came out.

00:42:14.560 --> 00:42:17.630
I know. I've been watching you.

00:42:18.840 --> 00:42:22.740
I see you trying, and I appreciate it more than you'll ever believe,

00:42:22.840 --> 00:42:26.940
but it's too big, even for you, Andy.

00:42:29.410 --> 00:42:29.970
It's an easy...

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:30.440
fix.

00:42:32.040 --> 00:42:33.220
What's more, it's what he wants.

00:42:37.410 --> 00:42:38.110
You know, the other day.

00:42:39.690 --> 00:42:40.410
He was talking to me.

00:42:41.220 --> 00:42:42.120
the girl that he likes.

00:42:44.230 --> 00:42:44.810
It wasn't much.

00:42:44.940 --> 00:42:45.820
talked for about an hour.

00:42:47.500 --> 00:42:48.200
But he was laughing.

00:42:51.240 --> 00:42:53.140
He was laughing. I hadn't seen him laugh since we got here.

00:42:56.650 --> 00:42:57.170
Yeah, the hell.

00:42:58.180 --> 00:42:58.640
I get him.

00:43:00.470 --> 00:43:01.270
And he gets me.

00:43:04.540 --> 00:43:04.860
Thank you.

00:43:05.910 --> 00:43:06.050
Thank you.

00:43:35.590 --> 00:43:36.570
Thank you.
